{
  "abstract": "The amplitude and phase for coherent regeneration in hydrogen and deuterium have been measured for six momentum bins in the range 3.5-10.5 GeV/c. Over this region the phase, \u03d5f, is consistent with being constant and has the value - 60\u00b0\u00b18\u00b0 for hydrogen and - 46\u00b0\u00b18\u00b0 for deuterium. Power-law fits of the form plabn for the amplitudes when combined with other data give n=\u22120.60\u00b10.02 for hydrogen and n=\u22120.52\u00b10.02 for deuterium.",
